WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.780
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday.

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:05.340
Today's video is like Plato's understanding of the human soul: It comes to you in three parts.

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.440
Part one: the small matter of giving away more than a million dollars

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.780
So, Hank, the 2015 Project for Awesome raised more than 1.5 million dollars, total.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.700
We don't know the final shipping costs for the perks, yet.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:20.220
so, I can't give out final numbers. But today, I do get to announce the winning charities.

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.440
Hank, I don't even know how to communicate my excitement about how well

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.060
the Project for Awesome went this year.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:27.660
Except to say that I am like Cheez-Doodles-guy excited about it.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:33.460
Ya! Yaaaaaaa! YeaaaaaAAH!

00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:34.380
God, I love Cheez Doodles guy!

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.920
So, during the first half of Project for Awesome, we raised more than a million dollars,

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.520
with the help of some matching donors to be split between

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.160
Save the Children and the UN's Refugee Agency

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.480
and, then, all the money raised during the second half of Project for Awesome goes to charities

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.600
chosen by the Nerdfighter community via voting at projectforawesome.com

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:54.900
So, the following ten charities got the most votes and will each receive 25 thousand dollar grants:

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.300
NaNoWriMo, which encourages creative writing and gives writing resources to schools and libraries;

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:00.980
The Against Malaria Foundation;

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.820
The Harry Potter Alliance, which turns fandoms toward activism;

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:06.600
This Star Won't Go Out, which provides direct support to families

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:08.460
who have a kid with cancer or another serious illness;

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:11.560
Liberty in North Korea, which assists North Korean Refugees and

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.380
fights to expose the Human Rights abuses there;

00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:17.000
water.org which provides sustainable clean water solutions to people around the world;

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.860
She's the First, which provides educational oppurtunities to girls in the developing world;

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.680
Planned Parenthood, which provides healthcare to women the United States

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.800
and, Action Against Hunger, which works to end hunger and malnutrition worldwide.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.240
And, then, Hank, the next ten most voted charities will receive smaller grants

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.960
but still more than ten thousand dollars.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.620
Those include: lava mae, Doctors without Borders, The Malala Fund, Uplift,

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:39.780
Direct, Relief, Not Forgotten, the Great Ormond Street Children's Hospital,

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:44.000
Soap Aid, charity: water,  and the American Foundation for Suicide Prevention.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.060
So, that's all where the money is going, thank you for donating,

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:51.200
again, all the charities were decided by your votes at projectforawesome.com. So, thanks for voting.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.780
Also, you can find more info about the charities in doobly-doo below

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:57.220
including a playlist with Project for Awesome videos about each of them.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.620
Part 2: Hank, our mom's artist friend, Connie Bostic, has made the greatest New Year's card of all time

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.620
and I wanted to share it with you. It's called

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.980
"We Must Live In Joy Through the Sorrows of this World."

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:07.120
No real story there. Just a great New Year's card.

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.220
Part 3: Hank, as this is my final vlogbrothers video of 2015

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:15.380
I must ask nerdfighteria four very important questions, to be addressed in the comments below:

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.580
1) What would you like to see more and/or less of, on vlogbrothers next year?

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:22.500
2) Should the rules change? 3) Should the schedule change?

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.620
And, 4) are you seriously going to punish me because my video about refugee camps

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:29.960
in Ethiopia was longer than four minutes, you horrible, hideous monsters?

00:02:29.960 --> 00:02:33.420
I tried really hard to frame that question in a non-partisan way. I think I pulled it off.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.940
Hank, I am off to go play FIFA as the AFC Wimbledon Wimbly-Womblies.

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.240
You can find that over at youtube.com/hankgames, where Hank doesn't play games.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:42.280
Happy New Year! Hank! I will see you on Friday.

